Most relevant tables & columns  

FORUMMESSAGEVOTES  
• "FromUserId": user who cast each up‑vote  
• "ToUserId"  : user who received each up‑vote  
• "ForumMessageId": the message that was up‑voted – lets us count “distinct” votes (one user may up‑vote several different messages of another user)  
• "Id": surrogate key, handy for fast counts when we do not need de‑duplication  
• "VoteDate": optional date filter if you want to restrict the time window  

USERS  
• "Id": joins to either "FromUserId" or "ToUserId"  
• "UserName": user login that the question asks us to display  
(You can also expose "DisplayName" if you prefer screen names.)  

Typical conditions we will use  
• GROUP BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId" to aggregate distinct up‑votes  
• COUNT(DISTINCT "ForumMessageId")         -- number of separate messages user A up‑voted for user B  
• JOIN USERS u1  ON u1."Id" = v."FromUserId"  
• JOIN USERS u2  ON u2."Id" = v."ToUserId"  
• LEFT JOIN ( …same aggregation with reversed columns… ) r ON … to find “up‑votes they gave back”  
• ORDER BY received_cnt DESC , gave_back_cnt DESC  
• LIMIT 1                                              -- only the very top pair  

Below are 10 progressive Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that explore the data step‑by‑step and finish with a final query that would return the requested result.  

```sql
-- 1) Peek at raw vote rows
--   Shows who voted for whom on which forum message.
SELECT "Id",
       "ForumMessageId",
       "FromUserId",
       "ToUserId",
       "VoteDate"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) How many total votes has each user GIVEN?
SELECT "FromUserId",
       COUNT(*)  AS "total_votes_given"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
GROUP  BY "FromUserId"
ORDER  BY "total_votes_given" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) How many total votes has each user RECEIVED?
SELECT "ToUserId",
       COUNT(*)  AS "total_votes_received"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
GROUP  BY "ToUserId"
ORDER  BY "total_votes_received" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Distinct votes from one user to another
--    Distinct by ForumMessageId (one user could vote several different messages).
SELECT "FromUserId",
       "ToUserId",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "ForumMessageId") AS "distinct_votes"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
GROUP  BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
ORDER  BY "distinct_votes" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Same as (4) but include usernames for readability
SELECT u_from."UserName" AS "from_user",
       u_to."UserName"   AS "to_user",
       COUNT(DISTINCT v."ForumMessageId") AS "distinct_votes"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES v
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u_from ON u_from."Id" = v."FromUserId"
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u_to   ON u_to."Id"   = v."ToUserId"
GROUP  BY u_from."UserName", u_to."UserName"
ORDER  BY "distinct_votes" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Prepare a derived table of counts A→B
WITH pair_counts AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId"  AS "giver",
           "ToUserId"    AS "receiver",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "ForumMessageId") AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
    GROUP  BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
)
SELECT *
FROM   pair_counts
ORDER  BY "votes_from_to" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Combine forward count and reverse count for each pair
WITH pair_counts AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId" AS "giver",
           "ToUserId"   AS "receiver",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "ForumMessageId") AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
    GROUP  BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
)
SELECT  pc1."giver"        AS "user_a",
        pc1."receiver"     AS "user_b",
        pc1."votes_from_to"        AS "a_to_b",
        COALESCE(pc2."votes_from_to",0) AS "b_to_a"
FROM    pair_counts pc1
LEFT JOIN pair_counts pc2
       ON pc2."giver"    = pc1."receiver"
      AND pc2."receiver" = pc1."giver"
ORDER BY pc1."a_to_b" DESC,
         COALESCE(pc2."votes_from_to",0) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same as (7) but attach usernames
WITH pair_counts AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId" AS "giver",
           "ToUserId"   AS "receiver",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "ForumMessageId") AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
